Subject: [gfx1151] do not trust prop.integrated on HIP

Upstream disabled the `integrated` fast path for CUDA "due to issues with
corrupted output (e.g. #15034)" but kept it enabled for HIP (PR #24233).
On this machine (Strix Halo, gfx1151, ROCm) that path corrupts the KV
state as soon as a SECOND slot is used: with -np 2 every answer after the
second prefix degenerates to '////' until the server restarts, sequential
or concurrent alike. Measured with bench/suites/slot-corruption.py; the
same test is clean on Vulkan and clean on ROCm with -np 1.

Matches llama.cpp #27579 (trigger: --parallel >= 2) and #27506, which
bisected a gfx1151 regression to the very commit that re-enabled this.

--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu
@@
-#if defined(GGML_USE_HIP)
-        info.devices[id].integrated = prop.integrated;
-#else
         info.devices[id].integrated = false; // Temporarily disabled due to issues with corrupted output (e.g. #15034)
-#endif
